{
  "dom_id": "step-q184240",
  "name": "Question 7",
  "problem": "Prove that  $3n-1$ is even whenever $n$ is odd.\n\nIf $n$ is odd, then $n=\\,${{field-1}} for {{field-2}}.\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n-1 & ={{field-3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $b=$ {{field-4}}. Since $a$ is {{field-5}}, we have that $b$ is {{field-6}}.\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3n-1 & ={{field-7}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich is a multiple of $2.$ Therefore, $3n-1$ is {{field-8}}.",
  "worked_solution": "",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
